			"widgets_values":[
				"Initial scene: The scene of the dilapidated wooden house from the original picture continues. Light from the broken hole in the roof creates a Tyndall effect. The man in black sits cross-legged on a grass mat, with a green glowing magic circle suspended behind him. The standing man holds a hot porridge and remains motionless.\nAction trigger: The man in black maintains a meditation posture. Only his right arm moves smoothly and effortlessly, swinging back and forth. The movement is fluid and carries a wind-like quality, and his sleeve robes puff up instantly with the force.\nSpecial effects presentation: When he swings, an invisible air wave is generated, causing the ground grass and the suspended kitchenware to shake violently; the standing man is instantly hit by the air wave and his body arcs towards the right side of the screen, flying out rapidly. His clothes and hair are blown backward by the air current, and the porridge bowl in his hand drops, spilling the hot porridge into the air.\nClosing shot: After the man in black finishes his gesture, he returns to the meditation posture, and the magic circle remains suspended. On the right side of the screen, only the empty door frame left after being flung away remains, intensifying the impact force.\nStyle requirement: Maintain the dark and martial-arts-themed feel of the original film, with smooth and natural movements. The air wave special effects should blend with the scene and avoid being overly exaggerated."
			],
